```java
class Workflow {
    Set<Transition> transitions;

    boolean canTransition(Issue issue, Status target) {
        return transitions.stream().anyMatch(t ->
            t.from.equals(issue.status) && t.to.equals(target));
    }

    void transition(Issue issue, Status target, User actor) {
        if (!canTransition(issue, target))
            throw new IllegalTransitionException(issue.status, target);
        issue.status = target;
        issue.history.add(new StatusChange(actor, issue.status, target, now()));
    }
}
```

`canTransition` is a lookup against this workflow's own `transitions` set — nothing here mentions a specific project or hardcodes which statuses exist. Two `Workflow` instances with entirely different `transitions` sets run through the exact same code.
